  "aiContextParagraph": "The Supreme Court of India has recently issued multiple bail orders involving political figures from the Aam Aadmi Party (AAP). Former AAP MLA Naresh Balyan was granted bail in a case involving the Maharashtra Control of Organised Crime Act (MCOCA), overturning a previous denial by the Delhi High Court. This decision was delivered by a bench consisting of Justices Vikram Nath and Aparesh Kumar Singh. Additionally, the court granted interim bail to another AAP leader, Deepak Singla, who is facing allegations in a bank fraud case valued at 155 crore rupees. These rulings represent significant legal developments for the party members involved, as the judiciary continues to process high-profile petitions concerning bail applications and criminal proceedings. The court's recent activity reflects an ongoing focus on the legal status and incarceration terms of individuals associated with various ongoing investigations in the country.",
